<script type="application/ld+json">
{
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "FAQPage",
  "mainEntity": [
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What are the best mental health apps in Australia?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "The best mental health apps available in Australia include BetterHelp (best for online therapy), Headspace and Calm (best for meditation), What's Up (best free all-rounder), and MindDoc (best for mood tracking). The right app depends on whether you need therapy, meditation, mood tracking, or a combination."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Are mental health apps in Australia free?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Many mental health apps have free tiers or free trials. What's Up and MindDoc offer fully free versions with decent feature sets. Headspace and Calm offer limited free content. BetterHelp requires a paid subscription but connects you with licensed therapists."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Can mental health apps replace therapy in Australia?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Mental health apps are best used as a complement to professional support, not a replacement — particularly for moderate to severe mental health concerns. Meditation and mood-tracking apps can be a helpful first step, but they do not provide the clinical diagnosis, personalised treatment plans, or duty of care that a registered psychologist provides."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Are mental health apps evidence-based?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "It varies. Apps that incorporate CBT (Cognitive Behavioural Therapy) techniques — like What's Up, BetterHelp, and MindDoc — have the strongest research backing. Meditation apps like Headspace and Calm have published peer-reviewed studies showing reductions in stress and anxiety. Always check whether an app cites clinical research rather than making generic wellness claims."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Is BetterHelp available in Australia?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Yes. BetterHelp is available in Australia and matches users with Australian-licensed therapists. All sessions are conducted via video, phone, or text chat. Pricing starts at around A$60-80/week (billed monthly), and you can cancel anytime. It's one of the most accessible ways to connect with a registered therapist from home."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What mental health apps are covered by Medicare in Australia?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Standard mental health apps are not Medicare rebatable. However, Australians with a Mental Health Care Plan can access up to 10 rebatable sessions with a registered psychologist through Medicare — a much more cost-effective option than most subscription apps. Speak to your GP to get a plan in place."
      }
    }
  ]
}
</script>

<Layout>
  <article>
    <div class="container article-body">
      <header class="article-header">
        <span class="category">Mental Health</span>
        <h1>Best Mental Health Apps in Australia (2025) — Honest Reviews</h1>
        <p class="description">We tested the most popular mental health apps available in Australia — here are our honest findings.</p>
      </header>

      <img
        src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1573496359142-b8d87734a5a2?w=1200&h=630&fit=crop&auto=format"
        alt="Person using a mental health app on their phone in a relaxed setting"
        class="article-hero-image"
        loading="lazy"
      />

      <div class="article-content">
        <div class="cta-box">
          <p>Looking for structured therapy from a licensed Australian professional? BetterHelp connects you with a therapist matched to your needs — often with your first session within 48 hours.</p>
          <a href="https://partners.betterhelp.com/go/referral/carevues" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Find a Therapist on BetterHelp →</a>
        </div>

        <p>Australians are increasingly turning to mental health apps as a first step — or a complement — to traditional support. Whether you're dealing with stress, anxiety, low mood, or just want to build better emotional habits, there's an app for that. But the quality varies enormously, and the wrong app can be a waste of money at best, and harmful at worst.</p>

        <p>We spent time testing the most-downloaded mental health apps available in Australia. Here's what actually works — and what doesn't.</p>

        <h2>Our Top Picks at a Glance</h2>

        <table>
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th>App</th>
              <th>Best For</th>
              <th>Price (AUD)</th>
              <th>Free Version</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr>
              <td><strong>BetterHelp</strong></td>
              <td>Online therapy with licensed professionals</td>
              <td>A$60–80/week</td>
              <td>No (free intro session)</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><strong>Headspace</strong></td>
              <td>Meditation and habit building</td>
              <td>A$69.99/year</td>
              <td>Limited starter pack</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><strong>Calm</strong></td>
              <td>Sleep and general relaxation</td>
